'''Clan Mudhorn''' was a [[Mandalorian]] [[Mandalorian clan|clan]] formed in the [[New Republic Era]]. It was composed of [[Din Grogu]], a [[Force-sensitive]] [[Mandalorian apprentice|Apprentice]], and [[bounty hunter]] [[Din Djarin]], who served as its leader. The [[Mandalorian]] clan's [[signet]] was the [[Bone|skull]] of a [[mudhorn]], which was bestowed upon them by [[the Armorer]] of [[the Tribe]]. The signet's design was in reference to the mudhorn creature that Djarin and Grogu killed on [[Arvala-7]].<ref name="Chapter 8" />

==History==
{{Quote|You're like a father to him.|[[Ahsoka Tano]] describes the relationship between Din Djarin and Grogu|<ref name="Chapter 13: The Jedi">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 13: The Jedi}}</ref>}}
[[File:Acme-TribeofTwo.png|thumb|left|260px|Din Djarin and Grogu, the two members of Clan Mudhorn.]]
Clan Mudhorn was a [[Mandalorian clan]]<ref name="Din Djarin">{{EncyclopediaCite|Din Djarin and Other Characters of the Underworld}}</ref> that was established during the [[New Republic Era]]. After [[Mission to Arvala-7|discovering]] a creature of an [[Yoda's species|unknown species]] named [[Din Grogu|Grogu]] on [[Arvala-7]], the [[Mandalorian]] [[Din Djarin]], a [[bounty hunter]], was seeking to take the bounty back to a client on [[Nevarro]].<ref name="Chapter 1">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 1: The Mandalorian}}</ref> Before he could do so, however, he found his ship, the ''[[Razor Crest]]'', taken apart by [[Jawa]]s. After tracking down the [[Jawa Sandcrawler]], he was offered his ship's parts in exchange for a [[mudhorn egg]]. After coming close to death at the hands of the [[mudhorn]], Djarin was saved when Grogu used [[the Force]].<ref name="Chapter 2">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 2: The Child}}</ref>

Later, in order to stop bounty hunters from the [[Bounty Hunters' Guild]] from capturing Grogu, Djarin, along with [[Greef Karga]], [[Carasynthia Dune|Cara Dune]], [[Kuiil]], and [[IG-11]], tracked down "[[The Client]]" on Nevarro. After a brief skirmish in the street, the group escaped into the sewer, where they found the Mandalorian [[Armorer]]. [[The Armorer]], acknowledging that Djarin and Grogu were now a [[Mandalorian clan|clan]] of two, crafted for them a mudhorn signet.<ref name="Chapter 8" />

After Grogu was [[Battle of Tython (9 ABY)|captured]] by the [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[Moff]] [[Gideon]] and his [[Gideon's Imperial remnant|remnant forces]], Djarin, [[Boba Fett]], Dune, bounty hunter [[Fennec Shand]] and Mandalorians [[Bo-Katan Kryze]] and [[Koska Reeves]] attempted to [[Incident on Nevarro|rescue]] Grogu. After defeating Gideon, the group was almost captured by [[Phase-III Dark Trooper|Dark Troopers]] but were rescued by [[Jedi Master]] [[Luke Skywalker]]. Following the rescue, Djarin gave Skywalker Grogu, in hopes that Grogu could be trained as a Jedi.<ref name="Chapter 16">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 16: The Rescue}}</ref> During this rescue, Djarin bested Moff Gideon in combat, gaining the fabled Mandalorian [[Darksaber]] for Clan Mudhorn. 

However, during Grogu's training, Skywalker sensed that the child's heart wasn't into relearning the Jedi path. After Djarin visited the planet bearing a gift of [[Grogu's chainmail shirt|chain mail armor]] for Grogu, Skywalker offered him with a choice: accepting the gift and returning to the Mandalorian, or taking [[Yoda's second lightsaber|Yoda's lightsaber]] and continue with his Jedi training.<ref name="Stranger">{{BOBF|Chapter 6: From the Desert Comes a Stranger}}</ref> Grogu chose to return to Djarin.<ref name="Honor">{{BOBF|Chapter 7: In the Name of Honor}}</ref> Djarin also accepted [[R5-D4]] as his co-pilot for his [[N-1 starfighter|N-1]] [[Din Djarin's N-1 starfighter|starfighter]] from [[Peli Motto]].<ref name="Ch. 18">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 18: The Mines of Mandalore}}</ref>

Following his reuinion with Grogu, the two scouted out the planet of Mandalore for the [[Mines of Mandalore]]. While searching, Djarin was bested in combat by a mechanical creature in the depths of the caves, effectively losing the right to the darksaber. 

After the reclamation of [[Mandalore]] by the Mandalorians, Din Djarin accepted the child, Din Grogu, as his apprentice and son, and moved back to Nevarro, working for the New Republic on contract jobs from [[New Republic]] Captain [[Carson Teva]].

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:FineArtPrints-Din-and-Grogu-Clan-of-Two.png|thumb|right|300px|A Sideshow Collectibles Art Print of Clan Mudhorn]]
The name "Clan Mudhorn" was first used in an article on [[StarWars.com]] advertising the release of the reference book ''[[The Star Wars Book]]'',<ref name="8 Secrets We Learned">{{SW|url=news/the-star-wars-book|text=8 Secrets and Fun Facts We Learned from ''The Star Wars Book''}}</ref> but the name was not used in the book itself. In its section on Mandalorian clans, it only places the word "Mudhorn" under the Mudhorn [[signet]].<ref name="SW Book">''[[The Star Wars Book]]''</ref> The name was confirmed to be [[canon]] when it was later used in "[[Din Djarin and Other Characters of the Underworld]]," a [[2021]] issue of the [[Star Wars Encyclopedia (series)|''Star Wars Encyclopedia'']].<ref name="Din Djarin" />

Clan Mudhorn is the subject of "Din Djarin & Grogu: A Clan of Two," an [[Sideshow Collectibles|Art Print]] by artist [[Jerry Vanderstelt]] released by [[Acme Archives Direct]] and [[Sideshow Collectibles]]. The image depicts Djarin and Grogu on an adventure<ref name="Clan of Two Print">{{SideshowCite|set=Sideshow Collectibles|pack=Din Djarin & Grogu: A Clan of Two|altlink=https://art.sideshow.com/art-prints/star-wars-din-djarin-grogu-a-clan-of-two-acme-archives-501320U}}</ref> sometime before the Battle of Tython<ref name="Clan of Two note">{{SideshowCite|set=Sideshow Collectibles|pack=Din Djarin & Grogu: A Clan of Two|altlink=https://art.sideshow.com/art-prints/star-wars-din-djarin-grogu-a-clan-of-two-acme-archives-501320U}} shows the ''[[Razor Crest]]'' and [[Din Djarin]]'s [[Amban phase-pulse blaster]], which are both destroyed in the [[Battle of Tython (9 ABY)|Battle of Tython]] seen in "[[Chapter 14: The Tragedy]]."</ref> after departing from the ''Razor Crest'', which remains landed close by as Djarin crouches down, with his pistol drawn and Grogu by his side.<ref name="Clan of Two Print" />

